#' Simulated Electronic Health Record (EHR) Longitudinal Data
#'
#' A pre-generated long-format longitudinal dataset with 2000 subjects,
#' designed to look like an outpatient EHR extract for HbA1c. The dataset
#' is generated by \code{\link{sim_data_gen}} using an EHR-style covariate
#' spec (Age, Gender, Marital, Black, Hispanic, NSES) and the back-transform
#' helper that adds raw and log-scale HbA1c outcome columns. The latent
#' factor \eqn{U_i}, frailty \eqn{\eta_i}, and per-process random effects
#' that the simulation generates internally are not retained in this
#' user-facing dataset, mirroring the situation in real EHR data.
#'
#' True parameter values used to generate the data are stored as an
#' attribute and can be retrieved with \code{attr(sim_ehr_data, "true_params")}.
#'
#' @format A \code{data.frame} with the following columns:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{id}{Integer subject identifier.}
#'   \item{Age}{Standardized age (z-score). Used by the modeling functions.}
#'   \item{Age_raw}{Age in years, drawn from \eqn{\mathrm{Uniform}(18, 99)}.
#'     Provided for descriptive summaries only; modeling functions should use
#'     \code{Age} (the standardized column).}
#'   \item{Gender}{Binary indicator (1 = male, 0 = female).}
#'   \item{Marital}{Binary indicator (1 = married, 0 = not).}
#'   \item{Black}{Binary indicator (1 = Black race, 0 = otherwise).}
#'   \item{Hispanic}{Binary indicator (1 = Hispanic ethnicity, 0 = otherwise).}
#'   \item{NSES}{Continuous neighborhood socioeconomic status indicator
#'     (standardized median household income; mean 0, SD 1).}
#'   \item{time}{Visit time on the 0 to 60 window. \code{NA} for subjects
#'     with no visits.}
#'   \item{R}{Observation indicator at the visit (1 = HbA1c recorded,
#'     0 = not recorded).}
#'   \item{Y}{Standardized linear outcome on which the data-generating
#'     model operates. Retained so analyses on the standardized scale (and
#'     comparison to the manuscript's simulation regime) are direct.
#'     \code{NA} when \code{R = 0}.}
#'   \item{HbA1c}{Raw HbA1c value, computed from \code{Y} via
#'     \code{exp(log(5.6) + 0.05 * Y)}. Distributed roughly in the range
#'     4.0 to 9.0. \code{NA} when \code{R = 0}.}
#'   \item{log_HbA1c}{Natural log of \code{HbA1c}. The recommended outcome
#'     for analysis, matching the convention used in
#'     Yang, Shi, and Mukherjee (2026). \code{NA} when \code{R = 0}.}
#'   \item{C}{Censoring time (end of follow-up window, 60 for all subjects).}
#' }
#'
#' @source Generated by \code{\link{sim_data_gen}} with the EHR-style
#'   covariate spec described in \code{data-raw/sim_ehr_data.R}, with
#'   \code{n = 2000}, \code{phi = 0}, and \code{seed = 2026}, then
#'   post-processed to add \code{HbA1c} and \code{log_HbA1c}.
#'
#' @examples
#' data(sim_ehr_data)
#' head(sim_ehr_data)
#'
#' # True data-generating parameters (named lists keyed by covariate name)
#' true <- attr(sim_ehr_data, "true_params")
#' true$beta
#'
#' @seealso \code{\link{sim_data_gen}} to generate new datasets with
#'   custom covariate sets and parameters.
"sim_ehr_data"
